--- Cut levels --------
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.MinAccumLevelToSave = -1 >   // minimum accum level to save the event

--- Systematics ------------

The single systematics configuration (when EnableSingle...SystConfigurations = 0)
or the all systematics configuration (when EnableAllSystematics = 0)
need to be enabled in baseAnalysis parameter file

--- Corrections -----------
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.ApplySCECorrection = 1 >

--- Systematics ------------
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.ApplySCESystematic = 0 >

--- Event Display ------------
 # Event display data is always saved to EventDisplayData tree for signal candidates.
 # This allows regeneration with full OpenGL zoom via DrawingTools::EvtDisplay()
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.CreateEventDisplay = 1 >

--- Annihilation Vertex Finder ------------
# Pairing threshold on daughter endpoint distance (cm); see AnnihilationVertexUseEndpointCombinatorics.
# When combinatorics is on, distance is the minimum over valid start/end pairs; when off, start–start only.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.AnnihilationVertexRadius = 10.0 >

# 1 = minimize distance over start/end combinations (SS/SE/ES/EE), then optionally reverse daughters for SE/ES/EE.
# 0 = plain start–start distance only; PairingEndpointCombo stays SS and no track reversal is applied.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.AnnihilationVertexUseEndpointCombinatorics = 0 >

# Radius used only for annihilation-vertex degeneracy counting (cm).
# It is only a loose preselection on raw PositionStart / early hits near the vertex.
# It does not affect vertex pairing or overlap filtering.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.AnnihilationVertexDegeneracyRadius = 10.0 >

# Maximum distance between the annihilation-vertex fit position and the candidate particle fitted line (cm).
< neutralKaonAnalysis.AnnihilationVertexDegeneracyLineToVertexDistance = 2.0 >
# Maximum distance between the closest point on the fitted line to the vertex and at least one projected PositionStart
# or projected early hit used as origin support for degeneracy counting (cm).
< neutralKaonAnalysis.AnnihilationVertexDegeneracyOriginSupportDistance = 5.0 >

# Minimum number of collection-plane hits required per daughter to create a vertex.
# Vertex is created only if both daughters satisfy NHitsPerPlane[2] > this value.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.AnnihilationVertexMinCollectionHits = 21 >

# Daughter PID veto when building annihilation vertex candidates (both daughters must pass).
# Reject if Chi2PID(2212) chi2/npts is strictly below this (proton template; same machinery as truth tree).
< neutralKaonAnalysis.AnnihilationVertexDaughterProtonChi2NdfRejectBelow = 50.0 >
# If not rejected above: reject if pion Chi2PID(211) chi2/npts is strictly above this (not pion-like enough).
< neutralKaonAnalysis.AnnihilationVertexDaughterPionChi2NdfRejectAbove = 25.0 >

--- Annihilation Line-Fit Parameters -----------
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.TrackFitLength = 25.0 > //length of track used for line fitting (cm)
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.TrackFitDistanceFromStart = 10.0 > //fit starts this many cm away from particle start position
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.VertexXBiasCorrectionCm = 1.0 > //x_corrected = x_reco - value (cm)

--- Creation Parent Tail Projection -----------
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.TrackFitCreationLength = 50.0 > //fit length used to build beam creation line (cm)
 < neutralKaonAnalysis.TrackFitDistanceCreationFromEnd = 15.0 > //fit starts this many cm backward from beam end
 # The tail segment used for projection is derived from TrackFitDistanceCreationFromEnd.

# Radius (cm) of the creation-candidate cylinder around the parent fitted line, from creation to annihilation position.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.CreationVertexRadius = 7.5 >
# Maximum distance between the creation-vertex reference position and a candidate particle fitted line (cm).
# Set to CreationVertexRadius default-equivalent to match current fallback behavior.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.CreationVertexLineToVertexDistance = 2.0 >
# Maximum distance between the closest point on the fitted line to the creation vertex and at least one projected
# PositionStart or projected early hit used as origin support for creation-degeneracy counting (cm).
# Set to 0.5 * CreationVertexLineToVertexDistance default-equivalent to match current fallback behavior.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.CreationVertexOriginSupportDistance = 5.0 >

# Keep second-particle candidates only if Chi2PID(2212) chi2/npts is <= this threshold (same as k0protonchi2ndfproton).
< neutralKaonAnalysis.CreationVertexSecondParticleMaxProtonChi2Ndf = 50.0 >

# Neutral candidates from annihilation vertices: when 1, keep at most one neutral per vertex (winner among parents).
# When 0, keep every neutral built for each qualifying parent (no per-vertex elimination).
< neutralKaonAnalysis.SelectSingleNeutralPerAnnihilationVertex = 1 >
# Creation-vertex beam-particle assignment mode:
# 0 = build all creation-vertex parent hypotheses, then compete.
# 1 = use the common reco parent of the two annihilation daughters as BeamParticle.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.CreationVertexBeamParticleMode = 1 >

--- ML residual-range dE/dx (annihilation pions) -----------
# Likelihood free-range scan tuned like arXiv:2409.18288 Table 1 (TLEFit, charged pions). Collection plane only.
# Minimum interior hits after skipping ends (before dE/dx window).
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FreeRangeDedxMinInteriorHits = 15 >
# Drop this many collection hits at track start and at track end before the fit.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FreeRangeDedxSkipHitsFirst = 3 >
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FreeRangeDedxSkipHitsLast = 3 >
# Keep hits with measured dE/dx in [Min, Max] MeV/cm (π hypothesis only; disabled for other PDG in code).
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FreeRangeDedxMinMeVcm = 0.5 >
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FreeRangeDedxMaxMeVcm = 5.0 >
# Scan additional track-length offset L in [0, Lmax] cm with this step (cm).
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FreeRangeScanLmaxCm = 450.0 >
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FreeRangeScanStepCm = 1.0 >
# Path length δx (cm) for Landau ξ in the hit PDF (paper uses ~0.65 cm typical 3D hit spacing in ProtoDUNE-SP).
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FreeRangeDedxPdfPathCm = 0.65 >

# Joint K0s-constrained ππ momenta (2D grid on |p1|,|p2| with soft m(K0s) penalty on interpolated free-range log L).
# 0 = disabled (each daughter: independent free-range ML as today). 1 = try joint; on failure falls back to independent.
# Validation: MC (P_reco-P_true)/P_true for joint vs independent; slice interacting vertices; stress-test bad opening angles.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.JointK0sMomentumEnable = 1 >
< neutralKaonAnalysis.JointK0sMomentumPMinGeV = 0.05 >
< neutralKaonAnalysis.JointK0sMomentumPMaxGeV = 7.0 >
< neutralKaonAnalysis.JointK0sMomentumPStepGeV = 0.05 >
# Gaussian mass prior width σ_M in MeV (converted to GeV internally).
< neutralKaonAnalysis.JointK0sMassSigmaMeV = 50.0 >
# Multiplier on 0.5*((M-m_K0s)/σ)^2; m_K0s fixed at 0.497611 GeV in code.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.JointK0sMassPenaltyScale = 1.0 >
# 1 = σ_m per event from (∂m/∂p_i σ_pi)^2 using TLE log L curvature at marginal maxima; 0 = fixed JointK0sMassSigmaMeV only.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.JointK0sMassSigmaEventPropagation = 1 >
# Second pass: step coarse / factor on a local box around the best cell; set 0 or 1 to disable refinement.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.JointK0sMomentumRefineFactor = 2 >

--- Momentum Assurance Parameters -----------
# Enable momentum assurance for signal codes only (1=only codes 1,5,6 / 0=all codes)
# Signal codes: 1=two_stopping, 5=one_stopping, 6=interacting
< neutralKaonAnalysis.EnsureMomentumSignalOnly = 1 >
# Enable writing momentum diagnostics: sigdedx, siglogl, joint 2D TH2s h_sigjoint2d, h_sigjointpen, h_sigjointlogl
# (S, mass penalty, logL1+logL2 TLE), marker TGraphs g_sigjoint2d_mrk_{tle,true,joint}_*, canvases c_sigjoint2d_*, c_sigjointpen_*, c_sigjointlogl_*.
# 1 = enabled, 0 = disabled.
< neutralKaonAnalysis.EnableMomentumDiagnosticMultigraphs = 1 >
# Fill extra free-range diagnostics (mean/sigma dE/dx bias Gaussian fit) for the per-daughter TLEFit path.
# 1 = enabled, 0 = disabled (faster, keeps these fields at sentinel values).
< neutralKaonAnalysis.FreeRangeComputeDedxBiasDiagnostics = 0 >

--- Other Parameters -----------

--- Event Skim File ------------
< baseAnalysis.StoreSurvivingEvents = 0 >  // Enable storing surviving events (0=disabled, 1=enabled)
 < baseAnalysis.TruthPDGForSkim = -1 >    // PDG code to check in truth (-1=disabled, e.g., 310 for K0)

###############################################################################
  baseAnalysis parameters
###############################################################################

This ia a copy of the baseAnalysis parameters file in highland, such that we can overwrite them


Whether to initialize trees or not at the beginning of each configuration

 < baseAnalysis.InitializeTrees = 1 >

 --- Corrections ------------

Disables all corrections regardless of the ones enabled below

 < baseAnalysis.Corrections.DisableAllCorrections  = 0 >

Apply all corrections even if they were already applied in the input file

 < baseAnalysis.Corrections.ForceApplyCorrections  = 0 >

Enable/Disable individual corrections


--- Event Weights ------------

Enable/disable configurations with a single systematic (when EnableSingleWeightSystConfigurations = 1)
and enable systematics in the "all_syst" configuration (when EnableAllSystematics = 1)

No weights yet !!!

--- Systematics ------------

Number of toy experiments
 < baseAnalysis.Systematics.NumberOfToys = 100 >

The Random Seed. When throwing toys we want the same random numbers for all jobs. Thus, the random seed should be the same in all cases (and different from 0 !!!!)

     0 --> A pure random seed is generated based on time
 not 0 --> A fix random seed is used

 < baseAnalysis.Systematics.RandomSeed = 1 >

Use a different random generator for each systematic

 < baseAnalysis.Systematics.IndividualRandomGenerator = 0 >


--- Configurations ------------

Create configurations with a single systematic ( a configuration for each systematic selected above)

 < baseAnalysis.Configurations.EnableSingleVariationSystConfigurations = 0 >
 < baseAnalysis.Configurations.EnableSingleWeightSystConfigurations    = 0 >

Enable/disable the configuration with all systematics (or the ones selected above)

 < baseAnalysis.Configurations.EnableAllSystematics = 0 >